{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1617","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1617","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1617\",\"parent_revision\":\"e629027a742a043d10220e0544ecf1217cd68edcd519ebc2e291acdab4bccf56\",\"root_revision\":\"e629027a742a043d10220e0544ecf1217cd68edcd519ebc2e291acdab4bccf56\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring a multi-agent task dispatch session (impl-confidence-scoring), T08 (t08-impl-manager-paths) completed and the agent reported completion, but SAM showed the task as `not-started`. The orchestrator had to call sam_state manually to correct the status before dependent tasks could unblock.\\n\\nObserved: agent terminates and reports done \u2192 SAM task status remains unchanged \u2192 orchestrator detects the mismatch \u2192 manually updates via sam_state \u2192 dependent tasks unblock.\\n\\nRoot cause unknown \u2014 could be: SubagentStop hook not firing, active-task session file not written (CLAUDE_SESSION_ID empty string issue documented in #1601), sam_state call in task-worker completion path not executing, or the task-worker agent using incorrect task_id on the update call.\\n\\nThis is related to the evidence gathered for #1601 (9 confirmed manual write instances across 7 sessions where agents bypass SAM state via filesystem). Need to trace whether T08 used the SubagentStop hook path or the inline sam_state call path, and why neither resulted in a status update.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] SubagentStop hook registered in `hooks/hooks.json`\\n- [ ] Agent completion triggers automatic status update to `complete` (verifiable via `sam_read`)\\n- [ ] Context file deleted after completion\\n- [ ] GitHub issue status syncs if `parent_issue_number` present in context (related: #1624)\\n- [ ] Reproduce #1617 scenario: task completes and status updates without manual orchestrator intervention\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **sam task status not updated when agent reports completion \u2014 orchestrator must manually correct** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Screenshot from claude_skills session \u2014 orchestrator log visible in Claude Code mobile app, 2026-04-06\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n- **Related**: #1624 (parent_issue_number missing in context), #1601\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Grooming\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### RT-ICA Snapshot (2026-04-07)\\n\\n**Goal:** Ensure agent task completion automatically updates SAM task status without orchestrator intervention.\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|-----------|--------|----------|\\n| Hook script implemented | AVAILABLE | `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` lines 582\u2013665 \u2014 fully implemented |\\n| Hook registered in hooks.json | MISSING \u2192 **this is the bug** | `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` registers only TaskCompleted/Stop/SessionEnd \u2014 no SubagentStop entry |\\n| Context file written by start-task | AVAILABLE | `skills/start-task/SKILL.md` lines 107\u2013123 document context file creation |\\n| Integration tests exist | AVAILABLE | `tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` |\\n| CLAUDE_SESSION_ID empty issue (#1601) | AVAILABLE | Documented in #1601; may cause context file created as `active-task-.json` |\\n\\n**Decision: APPROVED** \u2014 root cause is known, fix is clear.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type:** Defect \u2014 missing feature deployment (hook implemented but not wired)\\n\\n**5-Whys:**\\n1. Why doesn't task status update when agent completes? \u2192 SubagentStop hook never fires\\n2. Why doesn't it fire? \u2192 It is not registered in `hooks.json`\\n3. Why isn't it registered? \u2192 Hook script was implemented but the hooks.json wiring was omitted\\n4. Why was it omitted? \u2192 The implementation in `task_status_hook.py` was written but the deployment step (hooks.json entry) was not done\\n5. **Root fix:** Add SubagentStop entry to `hooks/hooks.json`\\n\\n**Pattern:** Recurring (#1601 pattern) \u2014 when hooks don't fire, agents observe stale state and bypass SAM via filesystem workarounds.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n| File | Role | Change needed |\\n|------|------|--------------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` | Hook registry | **ADD SubagentStop entry pointing to `task_status_hook.py`** |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` | Hook script | No change \u2014 already implemented at lines 582\u2013665 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` | Context file creation | No change \u2014 already writes context at lines 107\u2013123 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` | Fallback path | Lines 73\u201374 have inline completion path \u2014 verify it is still needed or can be removed |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_task_status_hook/test_subagent_stop_integration.py` | Integration test | Verify passes after hooks.json wired |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 **primary change location**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` (lines 582\u2013665)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/start-task/SKILL.md` (lines 107\u2013123)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` (lines 73\u201374)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Small (S)** \u2014 1\u20132 hours\\n- Implementation: add SubagentStop entry to hooks.json (0.25h)\\n- Validation: reproduce T08-style scenario to confirm status auto-updates (0.75h)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f4365e1ab03e84fd1b2151ee6e5222b081af602a7127cb592a0e974903f3074d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdroLQ\"}"}